# =============================================================================
# bing/web dev environment variables
# Copy this file to `.env.local` and fill in the values you need.
# Never commit `.env.local` or `.env` — they may contain real API keys.
# =============================================================================

# --- Database (SQLite) -------------------------------------------------------
# Path to the dev SQLite database file. The `db:init` script (and the auto-init
# that runs via `predev`) creates this file on first dev startup and applies
# the schema from `lib/database/schema.sql`. If unset, defaults to
# `<cwd>/data/binG.db` (see getDBPath() in lib/database/connection.ts).
#
# This is the source of truth for the dev DB. Keeping this file present (and
# non-empty) at first dev startup ensures the VFS ownerId can be resolved
# against a real `users` row — without it, VFS reads return null and the
# ownerId falls back to the literal string `'000'`, which causes cross-user
# workspace contamination after signup → logout → login.
DATABASE_PATH=./data/binG.db

# --- Encryption key (API keys at rest) --------------------------------------
# REQUIRED in production. In development a random per-session key is generated
# when this is unset, which means stored API keys do NOT survive a server
# restart. Set this to a 32+ character random string in `.env.local` to
# persist API keys across restarts.
#
# Generate one with: node -e "console.log(require('crypto').randomBytes(32).toString('hex'))"
# ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# --- Other dev settings ------------------------------------------------------
# See README.md for the full list of supported environment variables.
